<article class="env-lemma" id="0GL5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GL5">Lemma <span data-tag="0GL5">63.10.7</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a separated finite type morphism of quasi-compact and quasi-separated schemes. Let $\Lambda $ be a torsion ring. Let $E \in D(X_{\acute{e}tale}, \Lambda )$ and $K \in D(Y_{\acute{e}tale}, \Lambda )$. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  Rf_!E \otimes _\Lambda ^\mathbf {L} K = Rf_!(E \otimes _\Lambda ^\mathbf {L} f^{-1}K)  \]
</div>
  <p> in $D(Y_{\acute{e}tale}, \Lambda )$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose $j : X \to \overline{X}$ and $\overline{f} : \overline{X} \to Y$ as in the construction of $Rf_!$. We have $j_!E \otimes _\Lambda ^\mathbf {L} \overline{f}^{-1}K = j_!(E \otimes _\Lambda ^\mathbf {L} f^{-1}K)$ by Cohomology on Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/0GL1" data-tag="0GL1">21.20.9</a>. Then we get the result by applying Étale Cohomology, Lemma <a href="/tag/0F0G" data-tag="0F0G">59.96.6</a> and using that $f^{-1} = j^{-1} \circ \overline{f}^{-1}$ and $Rf_! = R\overline{f}_*j_!$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>